{"id":"hdf-libs-9d3","title":"Add input size limits to TypeScript converters for library use","description":"HIGH security finding: TS converters accept raw string input with no size validation when used as a library (not via CLI). The parseXml maxSize option exists but no converter uses it. A multi-GB input string could cause OOM.

Fix: Add configurable maxInputSize parameter to converter functions, or add a shared pre-check in converterutil.ts. The parseXml/parseJSON functions already support maxSize — converters should pass it through.

Mitigating factor: CLI enforces 50MB via readInputFile.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-03-03T03:46:49Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-03-03T03:46:49Z"}

{"id":"hdf-libs-3iu","title":"Validate CLI output path doesn't overwrite input","description":"MED security finding: writeConvertOutput writes to user-provided path with no validation. User could accidentally overwrite their input file (e.g., hdf convert nessus to hdf scan.xml scan.xml).

Fix: Check if output path matches input path and refuse (or warn). Consider --force flag for intentional overwrite.

