{"id":"hdf-libs-a3v","title":"Fix SonarQube fetcher silent response truncation","description":"MED security finding: SonarQube fetcher uses io.LimitReader without the +1 byte overflow detection used by GitLab and Splunk fetchers. If a response exceeds 10MB, it silently truncates producing an incomplete JSON body with a confusing parse error.

Fix: Use the readLimitedBody helper from the Splunk fetcher or apply the same +1 byte pattern from the GitLab fetcher.

